ures that characterize advanced Chinese; 2) exploring together with your classmates the different aspects of Chinese culture or events that interest\u00a0you by listening to the Chinese version of TED Talks; 3) completing a book or a magazine in Chinese as the group project documenting student learning during the semester.\u00a0 This course helps students further solidify their foundation for advanced-level study in Chinese, as well as enhance their awareness of and overall competence in cross-cultural communication.", "catalogBreadth": "(GB)", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "Satisfies Option 1.", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: students who have received at least a grade of B in CHIN 2209\u00a0or equivalent as determined through placement test.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2811, "crseId": 351064, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "CHIN", "catalogNbr": "3302", "titleShort": "High Intermediate Mandarin II", "titleLong": "High Intermediate Mandarin II", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 4277, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "09:05AM", "timeEnd": "09:55AM", "startDt": "01/24/2022", "endDt": "05/10/2022", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 5, "netid": "jl3275", "firstName": "Jyun-hong", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Lu"}], "pattern": "MTWRF", "facilityDescr": "Uris Hall G20", "bldgDescr": "Uris Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "URHG20", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Prerequisite: CHIN 3301 or plac